{"c":[{"id":"03207d6e6610e5a7","sum":"H1: Ask card reads facts blocks by first-row label (proposal.ts, golden ask-left.ndjson); swiftc typechecks Core without swift build. INT1: OWNER_NOTE_CHARS=0 behind TODO(INT1). PrivacyPromiseText.bundled reads PrivacyPromise.txt; the gate refuses a missing or other copy.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"150a341763717003","sum":"H1: the Ask card reads facts blocks by first-row label (proposal.ts YOU_TYPE_LABEL/LEFT_TO_YOU_LABEL via leftToYouBlocks, golden ask-left.ndjson). Swift typechecks without swift build via ~/.caret-run/bin/swift-typecheck <wt> --since <ref>.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T162304Z-08366a95f58a9161","text":"The Ask card reads a plan's facts blocks only by first-row label: proposal.ts YOU_TYPE_LABEL/LEFT_TO_YOU_LABEL, built in leftToYouBlocks and pinned by golden ask-left.ndjson; a new left-to-you block needs a label there (H1).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T162304Z-c9afd0b1b9d0e995","text":"Under HOLD, typecheck Swift without swift build: swiftc -emit-module CaretScreenCore into /tmp, then CaretHostCore via find (it has subdirs) with -I that dir; tests need the platform Developer Frameworks (-F) and -plugin-path .../host/plugins/testing (H1).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e3e2ae3d8390c6b7","sum":"OWNER_NOTE_CHARS is 0 behind TODO(INT1) (grep it to restore 2,000). Onboarding's privacyLine reads bundled PrivacyPromise.txt (nil under swift run/xctest; tests inject one); CARET_VERIFY_PRIVACY_RESOURCE refuses an app whose copy is missing or differs.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T030901Z-f494e5b78b4262d5","text":"INT1 (v2/int1): OWNER_NOTE_CHARS is 0 behind TODO(INT1) until HA2's allotment is re-expressed on the output-based ledger; the tests that need it are skipped or floored with TODO(INT1). grep TODO(INT1) to restore 2,000.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T053436Z-ced2cc8130be00ef","text":"Onboarding promise: PermissionsScreen.privacyLine reads bundle PrivacyPromise.txt (nil under swift run/xctest); renders and tests inject their own PrivacyPromise. CARET_VERIFY_PRIVACY_RESOURCE: gate refuses a finished app whose copy is missing, empty or not PRIVACY_PROMISE.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1eef6f94513579f4","sum":"Ask stand-ins read labels via test/builders.ts scopeLabel, never by regex; an askAnswer with no picks is valid only beside filling labels. HI2: no -- in Info.plist comments (the gate parses XML); VM build.sh needs the commit on v2/host; cp -cR of a symlinked node_modules dangles.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"3a15d551c65db7c1","sum":"Elapsed-time candidate cuts made the canned Ask oracle load-sensitive. Scope-ask stand-ins use builders.scopeLabel, never wording regexes. An askAnswer with no picks is valid only beside a question's filling labels.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T080402Z-28411e2e4fbdeba1","text":"realfill-asks canned oracle: fill's 15 ms wall-clock candidate budget (GENERATOR_BUDGET_MS) flips a single run's Ask right->refused about 1 in 20 under load; rerun or loop one Ask before calling an oracle drop a regression (G35 b31-04, ask-17).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T080402Z-5b6ab755f2bbf6d7","text":"Scope-ask stand-ins read the field label with test/builders.ts scopeLabel (wording: Field: \"<label>\". Control: ...); never regex the wording in a test. An askAnswer with no picks is valid only beside a question's filling labels.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c6064da85f9f18d6","sum":"HI2: the privacy gate parses Bundle/Info.plist as XML, so -- inside an XML comment fails every build. VM harness build.sh (h11/h13/h14) exports from a fixed worktree, needs the commit on v2/host, and cp -cR of a symlinked node_modules leaves a dangling link.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T080815Z-40413337304fea62","text":"The privacy gate parses apps/caret/Bundle/Info.plist as XML, so a double hyphen inside an XML comment refuses every build-app.sh mode (v2/onboard-privacy ccff2558 rewords it; HI2).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T080815Z-5040e69897a0bba9","text":"VM harness build.sh (h11/h13/h14) exports from a hardcoded worktree W, requires the commit on v2/host, and clones W's node_modules with cp -cR, which copies a symlinked node_modules as a dangling link (HI2).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
